# Aditya-L1 Solar Flare Forecasting – Project Overview

This document provides a simple, complete report on all the Python files in your workspace and explains how they work together to form the Solar Flare Forecasting system.

---

## 🚀 How to Run the Pipeline

The central entry point for the machine learning pipeline is **`flare_forecast/main.py`**. You execute this file using the Python interpreter inside your virtual environment (`.venv312`).

### 1. To Train the Model
This will load the data, process it, train the LSTM neural network, evaluate it, and generate SHAP explainability plots.
```bash
.venv312\Scripts\python.exe -m flare_forecast.main train
```

### 2. To Run a Prediction (Operational Forecast)
This will use the previously trained model and the latest available data to output a live probability forecast and operational risk level.
```bash
.venv312\Scripts\python.exe -m flare_forecast.main forecast
```

