## 📁 Core Machine Learning Package (`flare_forecast/`)

These files form the core deep learning pipeline. They are designed to be imported as a module and are executed via `main.py`.

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| **`main.py`** | The **Command-Line Interface (CLI)**. This is the master script you execute. It routes your commands (`train`, `evaluate`, `forecast`) to the appropriate modules below. |
| **`config.py`** | The central **Configuration Hub**. Contains all hyperparameters (window size, epochs, learning rate, thresholds) and file paths. Edit this file to change how the model behaves. |
| **`dataset.py`** | **Data Loader**. Responsible for reading the raw `.fits` (FITS) files from the SoLEXS and HEL1OS instruments, cleaning them, and merging them into a synchronized timeline. |
| **`feature_engineering.py`** | **Feature Creator**. Extracts mathematical properties from the raw data (like rolling means, gradients, and volatility) to give the neural network better context. |
| **`preprocessing.py`** | **Data Preparation**. Handles missing values, scales the data (StandardScaler), and slices the timeline into sliding "windows" (sequences) that the LSTM model requires. |
| **`model.py`** | **Neural Network Architecture**. Defines the architecture of the deep learning model (LSTM + Bahdanau Attention). This is where the mathematical structure of the AI is written. |
| **`trainer.py`** | **Training Loop**. Contains the logic for actually training the model. It handles Class Weights (to balance rare X-class flares against the Quiet Sun), Early Stopping, and saving the best model checkpoint. |
| **`evaluate.py`** | **Testing & Metrics**. After training, this file calculates scientific metrics like True Skill Statistic (TSS), Accuracy, F1-Score, and Heidke Skill Score (HSS) to prove the model works. |
| **`explain.py`** | **Explainability (SHAP)**. Analyzes the trained model to understand *why* it makes certain predictions, determining which features (e.g., SoLEXS gradient) are most important. |
| **`predict.py`** | **Operational Forecasting**. Contains the `OperationalForecaster` class. It loads the pre-trained model and runs real-time inference to spit out the current Solar Flare probabilities and Risk Level. |
| **`visualize.py`** | **Plotting**. Contains all the functions that draw graphs (ROC curves, Confusion Matrices, Prediction Timelines) and save them as `.png` files. |
| **`utils.py`** | **Helper Tools**. Contains generic background tools like file saving/loading, logging setup, and random seed fixing. |
| **`_tf_check.py`** | **Safety Check**. A simple script that ensures TensorFlow is installed correctly and warns you if you are using an incompatible Python version. |

