## 📂 Exploratory Data Analysis & Utilities (Root Directory)

These files reside in the main `c:\Users\anand\ISRO,BHA\` folder. They are mostly standalone scripts used for inspecting data, debugging, and initial research before the formal AI pipeline was built.

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| **`solar_flare_eda.py`** | A massive, comprehensive script for **Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)**. It reads the raw solar data and generates exploratory charts to understand the underlying physics. |
| **`flare_detection.py`** | An independent script built to visualize X-ray data and explicitly draw annotations on the peaks of solar flares based on threshold baseline multipliers. *(Note: This is the file you were just running).* |
| **`raw_data_viewer.py`** | A utility script that parses the raw FITS data and dumps it into a readable text format so a human can inspect the raw structure and metadata. |
| **`inspect_fits.py` & `inspect_fits2.py`** | Small debugging scripts used to open individual FITS files and print out their internal Header Data Units (HDUs) and table schemas. |
| **`check_env.py`** | A diagnostic script that verifies your Python environment, listing installed packages and ensuring your hardware/software stack is ready for machine learning. |
| **`fix_unicode.py`** | A tiny script likely used to strip bad characters or fix encoding issues in text/CSV files. |

